---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '../components/global/Button.astro';
import NatureIcon from '../components/global/NatureIcon.astro';
import LeafFlourish from '../components/global/LeafFlourish.astro';
import LeafDivider from '../components/global/LeafDivider.astro';
const reasons = [
  ['Our Core Values', `Participants are encouraged to see themselves as part of the web of life
Practice gratitude, land acknowledgement, and sit spot
Explore self-awareness
Build relationships and community
Connect with the earth
Become more mindful of where things come from and where things go
Cultivate leadership skills
Be called to social action`],
  ['Leadership Development', `Identifying the challenges that our world and communities face is the easy part. Learning how to take steps to address issues like climate change and structural racism takes grit and guts. Developing small and measurable group goals, we learn to move from identifying a problem to forming and implementing a solution. Wayfinders participants bring these skills to their communities to make a larger impact.`],
  ['Community Building & Social Justice', `How do we create the community we want to be part of? The Wayfinders community is a microcosm of our larger community and a playground for defining the values that we want to live by. Exploring how our family and personal values align (or don’t align) with the kind of community we want to live in helps participants find their way to taking the steps to transform their communities.

We look at our community with fresh eyes, trying to understand the systems and structures all around us that have led to profound inequality. And we consider organizing and leadership opportunities to overcome these barriers.`],
  ['Adolescence to Adulthood', `The adolescent stage is where the term “identity crisis” originated. Adolescents stop looking to their parents/guardians for guidance and instead look toward their peers and other adults. The “social brain” activates as they start orienting towards the bigger world. Individuation is front and center during this developmental time. Wayfinders are surrounded by skilled mentors and a supportive peer group, where genuine and positive identities have a chance to evolve. Participants at Wayfinders will find relevance and meaning through self-driven experiences and project based learning.`],
  ['Safe Space, Belonging', `Humans are social beings, wired for membership in a group. When children are consumed by monitoring their environment for cues of rejection, they can’t take in new information. Social media is a cesspool for rejection - kids feel left out when they see gatherings that they are not included in and are subjected to constant comparison as they scroll through their feeds. This onslaught of rejection impacts self-confidence and creates vulnerability to mental illness.

Wayfinders are encouraged to be their most authentic selves as they explore the big questions of who they are, how they relate to people, and what they want to contribute to the world. Participants will thrive in a culture of kindness, where they feel safe and a sense of belonging.`],
  ['Technology, Social Media, COVID, the Climate Crisis', `Our children spend more time indoors and on screens and are more isolated than they have ever been. Children spend 3-7 hours a day on screens and miss out on childhood experiences necessary for healthy development. Depression, anxiety, and suicide rates are on the rise and scientific evidence makes it clear that there are long-tem detrimental impacts on the brain. The climate crisis is real, and our kids (and all of us) are unclear about the inevitable shifts. Children today may need a different skill set to succeed in the new world than those that we were prepared for. The scientific evidence is clear- spending time outdoors, in nature, improves overall mental health. Therapists are prescribing time in nature rather than medication. Wayfinders gather in the woods and spend time bonding and sharing around fire circles where we slow down and feel the beauty of connecting with ourselves, each other, and the natural world. We practice survival skills that build our relationship with the elements as we explore animal tracking, shelter and fire building, plant, tree, and mushroom identification, and earth crafts.`],
  ['Your Child’s Future', `Transformative experiences during this stage of life, sets the stage for the future. EQ (Emotional Quotient) is now understood as a better indicator of success than IQ (Intelligence Quotient) and is used to identify leaders, good team players, and people who work well independently.

Wayfinders experiences sharpen EQ through social emotional learning, team building, nature connection, leadership development, and exercise. Wayfinders infuses soft and hard skills necessary to help navigate the social world and increase resilience. Learning to self-monitor and regulate emotions will have positive lifelong impacts.`],
  ['Rites of Passage', `In today’s busy world, we find that we are often rushing from one activity to the next. In this scenario, life starts to feel like a run on sentence, without punctuation or time for breath. Between school, extracurriculars, busy weekends, and non-stop technology, we are running ragged and often failing to pause for reflection, celebration, or re-calibration.

Rites of passage serve as a way of pausing and honoring significant milestones as we transition from one stage into another. Ceremonies allow us to hold space for these moments and make them stand out as special, beautiful, meaningful, and memorable. Wayfinders experience rites of passage in group and individual ceremonies and recognize the significance of their personal growth and their impact on the larger community.`],
];
const reasonIcons = ['leaf','community','heart','feather','community','mountain'] as const;
const gallery = [
 ['https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/61532ef9082b334755993cfd/f4fe7b2e-c144-4a34-80e9-e2cc36020dbb/IMG_9824.jpg?format=1200w','Wayfinders participants spending time together in the woods'],
 ['https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/61532ef9082b334755993cfd/789b6d2c-2c18-4deb-bb72-77c490b848a1/IMG_9803.jpg?format=1200w','Wayfinders outdoor nature activity'],
 ['https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/61532ef9082b334755993cfd/263cf156-497a-437a-a4b2-dc628ab6ff0d/michaeala.jpg?format=1200w','Wayfinders participant outdoors'],
 ['https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/61532ef9082b334755993cfd/86eadd05-5ce1-40af-bdad-9a5c43c6be5d/Drawing+with+charcoal.jpeg?format=1200w','Drawing with charcoal during a Wayfinders activity'],
 ['https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/61532ef9082b334755993cfd/97cf9aeb-fa20-4b44-94dd-2e5017f7b3bd/43-Alice+Gwen+candle.jpeg?format=1200w','Wayfinders ceremony with a candle'],
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Wayfinders on the Hudson" description="Screen-free nature programs that connect people with themselves, each other, and the earth.">
  <section class="hero home-hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <h1>Connecting<br />With Ourselves,<br />Each Other,<br />And the Earth</h1>
      <p class="hero-tagline">Screen-free time in nature. Programs for people of all ages.</p>
      <div class="hero-program-actions"><h2>Check out our NEW programs!</h2><div class="actions"><Button href="/fall-2026-programs-overview">Explore fall programs</Button><Button href="/our-mission" variant="secondary">Our mission</Button></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="what-is chapter">
    <div class="wide"><div class="what-panel"><h2>What is Wayfinders?</h2><p>We are living at a time when we are increasingly disconnected with ourselves, each other, and the earth. Wayfinders offers a solution: Mindfulness, community building, and nature immersion. Through social emotional learning and sustainability practices, Wayfinders provides experiential opportunities to disconnect (from technology) and reconnect with ourselves, each other, and the earth.</p><div class="what-gallery"><img src="/images/content/fire3.jpg" alt="Wayfinders participants gathered around a fire" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" /><img src="/images/content/tea-fire-1.jpg" alt="Tea prepared beside a fire outdoors" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" /><img src="/images/content/walk-team-1.jpg" alt="Wayfinders team walking together outdoors" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" /></div><p>Wayfinders creates a fun & safe space to build interconnectedness through nature guided experiences and social & emotional mentoring. The program explores leadership development and community building, and offers Junior Mentor or Mentor-in-Training programs; and for those interested - Rites of Passage.</p><p>Wayfinders experiential opportunities with nature connection and social emotional learning result in positive impacts including:</p><ul><li>shaping future sustainability advocates</li><li>addressing mental health challenges</li><li>increasing opportunities for diverse and underserved participants.</li></ul></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="base-camp chapter">
    <div class="wide"><div class="base-camp-content"><p class="type-label">Now enrolling</p><h2>Fall 2026 Base Camp</h2><div class="base-camp-copy"><p>Wayfinders Base Camp ignites a love for nature and fosters social-emotional learning through:</p><div class="base-camp-highlights"><article><NatureIcon name="fire" size={33} /><h3>Weekly Fire Circles &amp; Nature Games</h3><p>Deepen connections with the outdoors and each other through engaging activities.</p></article><article><NatureIcon name="heart" size={33} /><h3>Social-Emotional Learning</h3><p>Build confidence, communication skills, and empathy in a supportive environment.</p></article><article><NatureIcon name="community" size={33} /><h3>Community Building</h3><p>Create lasting friendships and a sense of belonging within a caring group.</p></article></div><div class="base-camp-scheduling"><p class="base-camp-subheading">Flexible Scheduling &amp; Growth for All Ages</p><div class="base-camp-schedule-grid"><article><NatureIcon name="calendar" size={31} /><h3>Choose Your Day</h3><p>Weekly after-school sessions on Tuesdays, Wednesdays, Thursdays or (or pick two or all three days for a 10% discount).</p></article><article><NatureIcon name="community" size={31} /><h3>Same &amp; Mixed-Age Groups</h3><p>In mixed-age groups, younger children find role models in older kids, while older ones develop leadership skills by mentoring their peers.</p></article></div></div></div><Button href="/fall-2026-base-camp-k-8">Discover Base Camp <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></Button></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="why chapter">
    <div class="wide"><header class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow-line type-label">The call to action</p><h2>Why Wayfinders?</h2><p>Why did climate activist Gwen Merkin and School Counselor Leah Gozhansky create Wayfinders on the Hudson? After 30 years of combined experience, the evidence of a need for this program is very clear! Click on the sections below to learn more.</p></header><div class="reason-grid">{reasons.slice(0,6).map(([title, copy], index) => <details class={`reason reason-${index + 1}`} open={index === 0}><summary><h3>{title}</h3><span class="reason-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="reason-content">{index === 0 ? <ul class="core-values">{copy.split('\n').map((value) => <li><NatureIcon name="check" size={25} /><span>{value}</span></li>)}</ul> : <p>{copy}</p>}</div></details>)}</div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="statements"><div class="wide"><p>Our children are disconnecting from themselves, their families, communities, and the earth as they enter their teenage years.</p><p>Wayfinders carves out time for youth to step away from the daily, to connect with purpose.</p><LeafDivider class="statements-divider" /></div></section>

  <section class="future chapter"><LeafFlourish side="right" variant="big-3" class="future-leaf" /><div class="wide future-grid"><header><p class="type-label">Growing up. Growing together.</p><h2>Real-world experiences for a life of purpose.</h2></header>{reasons.slice(6).map(([title, copy]) => <article><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></article>)}<div class="gallery">{gallery.slice(0,3).map(([src,alt]) => <img {src} {alt} width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" />)}</div></div></section>

  <section class="land chapter"><div class="wide land-grid"><div><p class="type-label">Land Acknowledgment and Responsibility</p><h2>We recognize the enduring stewardship of the Lenape.</h2></div><p>The Wayfinders team recognizes that the land where we live, work and play exists within the territory of the Lenape. We acknowledge the Lenape for their enduring stewardship of this place throughout the centuries and still today. We recognize a responsibility to learn about this history while educating new generations about how to live in right relationship with the earth and all of her inhabitants. Learning and relationship building is an ongoing pursuit and we welcome guidance and feedback from all as we endeavor to repair and restore this relationship.</p></div></section>

  <section class="connect chapter"><div class="wide connect-grid"><div><p class="type-label">Stay connected</p><h2>Let’s meet up in real life to share in the beauty of the natural world.</h2></div><div><h3>Join Our Mailing List</h3><p>Sign up with your email address to receive news and updates.</p><Button newsletter>Join our mailing list <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></Button></div><div><p>Sign up to be the first to know about our events.</p><p><a href="mailto:wayfindersonthehudson@gmail.com">wayfindersonthehudson@gmail.com</a><br />(917) 318-3888</p><Button href="/fall-2026-programs-overview">Our Programs</Button><div class="event-signup"><Button newsletter variant="secondary">Get program updates <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></Button></div></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .chapter{padding-block:clamp(5rem,10vw,9rem)}.wide{width:min(calc(100% - 2 * var(--gutter)),var(--width-wide));margin-inline:auto}.hero{position:relative;display:grid;min-height:min(47rem,82vh);align-items:center;isolation:isolate;background:url('/images/heroes/home-leaves-1.jpg') center 43%/cover no-repeat;color:#fff}.hero::after{position:absolute;z-index:-1;inset:0;content:'';background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgb(8 25 15/.9),rgb(8 25 15/.62) 52%,rgb(8 25 15/.12))}.hero-inner{width:min(calc(100% - 2 * var(--gutter)),var(--width-wide));margin:auto;padding-block:5rem}.hero h1{max-width:46rem;margin:0;color:#fff;font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:calc(clamp(3.6rem,7vw,6.4rem) + var(--font-display-size-adjust) + var(--font-display-hero-size-adjust));font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.04em;line-height:.92}.hero-tagline{margin:1rem 0 0;color:#e3dda3;font-family:var(--font-hand);font-size:calc(clamp(1.7rem,3vw,2.4rem) + var(--font-hand-size-adjust));line-height:1.05}.hero-program-actions{margin-top:45px}.hero h2{margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#fff;font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:calc(clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.2rem) + var(--font-display-size-adjust));font-weight:500}.actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.75rem;margin-top:2rem}.hero .actions :global(.button.primary){border-color:#fff;background:#fff;color:var(--color-forest-dark)}.hero .actions :global(.button.secondary){border-color:#fff;color:#fff}.split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.05fr;gap:clamp(3rem,7vw,6rem);align-items:center}.base-camp,.future{position:relative;overflow:hidden}.base-camp>*:not(.leaf-flourish),.future>*:not(.leaf-flourish){position:relative;z-index:1}.base-camp-leaf{top:10%;}.future-leaf{bottom:5%;}.base-camp{background:#fbf8f0}.base-camp figure{overflow:hidden;aspect-ratio:1/.92;margin:0;border-radius:var(--radius-card)}.base-camp img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover}.eyebrow-line{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.7rem;color:var(--color-rust)}.eyebrow-line::before{width:1.5rem;border-top:1px solid currentColor;content:''}.base-copy h2,.what-panel h2,.section-heading h2,.future h2,.land h2,.connect h2{margin:.45rem 0 1.25rem;color:var(--color-forest-dark);font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:calc(clamp(2.6rem,4.8vw,4rem) + var(--font-display-size-adjust));font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.03em;line-height:1}.base-copy>p,.feature-list{font-size:.94rem}.feature-list{display:grid;gap:.55rem;padding:0;list-style:none}.feature-list li{position:relative;padding-left:1.4rem}.feature-list li::before{position:absolute;left:0;color:var(--color-moss);content:'◆';font-size:.6rem;top:.35rem}.what-is{display:flex;align-items:center;min-height:45rem;padding-inline:var(--gutter);background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgb(18 42 28/.12),rgb(18 42 28/.05)),url('https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/61532ef9082b334755993cfd/f4fe7b2e-c144-4a34-80e9-e2cc36020dbb/IMG_9824.jpg?format=1500w') center/cover}.what-panel{width:min(43rem,100%);margin-left:max(0px,calc((100vw - var(--width-wide))/2));padding:clamp(2rem,5vw,4rem);border-radius:var(--radius-card);background:rgb(255 253 247/.96);box-shadow:var(--shadow-soft)}.what-panel p,.what-panel li{color:var(--color-ink-muted)}.why{background:#fbf8f0}.section-heading{max-width:58rem;margin:0 auto 3.5rem;text-align:center}.section-heading .eyebrow-line{justify-content:center}.section-heading p:last-child{color:var(--color-ink-muted)}.reason-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1rem}.reason{border:1px solid var(--color-line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);background:var(--color-surface);box-shadow:0 8px 24px rgb(23 59 42/.05)}.reason summary{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr auto;gap:1rem;align-items:center;min-height:7.5rem;padding:1.4rem;cursor:pointer;color:var(--color-forest-dark);font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:calc(1.45rem + var(--font-display-size-adjust));font-weight:600;line-height:1.05;list-style:none}.reason summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}.reason-icon{display:grid;width:3.4rem;aspect-ratio:1;place-items:center;border-radius:50%;background:var(--color-moss);color:#fff}.reason-2 .reason-icon,.reason-5 .reason-icon{background:#387493}.reason-3 .reason-icon,.reason-6 .reason-icon{background:#b75a19}.plus{font-family:var(--font-sans);font-size:1.4rem}.reason[open] .plus{transform:rotate(45deg)}.reason p{margin:0;padding:0 1.5rem 1.5rem;color:var(--color-ink-muted);font-size:.9rem;white-space:pre-line}.future{background:linear-gradient(110deg,#e9ede3,#faf7ee)}.future-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.75fr 1fr 1fr;gap:clamp(2rem,4vw,4rem);align-items:start}.future header{grid-column:1/-1}.future header h2{max-width:48rem}.future article{padding-right:2rem;border-right:1px solid var(--color-line)}.future h3{font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:calc(2rem + var(--font-display-size-adjust));line-height:1.1}.future article p{color:var(--color-ink-muted);white-space:pre-line}.gallery{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:.75rem}.gallery img{width:100%;height:100%;min-height:20rem;object-fit:cover;border-radius:var(--radius-card)}.statements{padding-block:clamp(3rem,6vw,5rem);background:var(--color-cream)}.statements .wide{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:var(--column-gap)}.statements p{margin:0;color:var(--color-forest-dark);font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:calc(clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.6rem) + var(--font-display-size-adjust));font-weight:600;line-height:1.1}:global(.statements-divider){grid-column:1/-1}.land{background:var(--color-forest-dark);color:#fff}.land-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;gap:clamp(3rem,7vw,7rem);align-items:center}.land .type-label{color:#d8d095}.land h2{color:#fff}.land-grid>p{font-size:1.05rem}.connect{background:#fbf8f0}.connect-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:clamp(2rem,5vw,4rem);align-items:start}.connect h2{font-size:calc(clamp(2.5rem,4vw,3.6rem) + var(--font-display-size-adjust))}.connect h3{font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:calc(1.8rem + var(--font-display-size-adjust))}.event-signup{margin-top:1.5rem}
  .hero{min-height:calc(min(47rem,82vh) + 9.0625rem)}.hero-inner{transform:translateY(4.375rem)}
  @media(max-width:63.999rem){.split,.land-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.reason-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.future-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.gallery{grid-column:1/-1}.connect-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.connect-grid>div:first-child{grid-column:1/-1}}
  @media(max-width:47.999rem){.hero{min-height:42rem;background-position:62% center}.hero::after{background:rgb(8 25 15/.7)}.hero h1{font-size:calc(clamp(3.25rem,15vw,5rem) + var(--font-display-size-adjust) + var(--font-display-hero-size-adjust))}.actions{flex-direction:column}.actions :global(.button){width:100%}.reason-grid,.future-grid,.statements .wide,.connect-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.future header,.gallery,.connect-grid>div:first-child{grid-column:auto}.future article{padding:0 0 2rem;border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-line)}.gallery{grid-template-columns:1fr}.gallery img{min-height:15rem}.what-is{background-position:60% center}.what-panel{padding:2rem}.reason summary{min-height:6rem}.land-grid{gap:1rem}}
  @media(max-width:47.999rem){.hero{min-height:calc(42rem + 9.0625rem)}}
  @media(min-width:48rem){.hero::after{background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgb(8 25 15/.9) 0%,rgb(8 25 15 / 0) 85%)}}

  /* Home-page sequence: quiet introduction, then the fuller case for Wayfinders. */
  .what-is{display:block;min-height:0;padding-inline:0;background:var(--color-surface)}
  .what-panel{width:100%;max-width:var(--width-wide);margin-inline:auto;padding:0;border-radius:0;background:transparent;box-shadow:none;text-align:center}
  .why{background:linear-gradient(110deg,#e9ede3,#faf7ee)}
  .reason-grid{align-items:stretch}
  .reason{padding:clamp(1.25rem,2.2vw,2rem)}
  .reason-heading{display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:center}
  .reason h3{margin:0;color:var(--color-forest-dark);font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:calc(clamp(1.45rem,2vw,1.9rem) + var(--font-display-size-adjust));font-weight:600;line-height:1.05}
  .reason p{margin:1.25rem 0 0;padding:0;color:var(--color-ink-muted);font-size:1.1875rem;line-height:1.65;white-space:pre-line}
  .what-gallery{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1rem;margin:2.25rem 0}
  .what-gallery img{width:100%;height:clamp(11rem,18vw,16rem);object-fit:cover;border-radius:var(--radius-card)}
  @media(max-width:47.999rem){.what-gallery{grid-template-columns:1fr}.what-gallery img{height:15rem}}

  .base-camp{display:flex;align-items:center;min-height:54rem;background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgb(10 27 17 / .92) 0%,rgb(10 27 17 / .73) 43%,rgb(10 27 17 / .08) 78%),url('/images/banners/running-kids-3.jpg') center / cover no-repeat;color:white}
  .base-camp-content{position:relative;left:-75px;z-index:1;max-width:min(100%,calc(60% + 10vw))}
  .base-camp .type-label{margin:0;color:#e4dda2;font-family:var(--font-hand);font-size:calc(clamp(1.9rem,3vw,2.5rem) + var(--font-hand-size-adjust));font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0;text-transform:none}
  .base-camp h2{margin:.45rem 0 1.5rem;color:white;font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:calc(clamp(3.8rem,6.5vw,6rem) + var(--font-display-size-adjust));font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.04em;line-height:.9}
  .base-camp-copy{display:grid;gap:25px}
  .base-camp-copy p{margin:0;font-size:1.1875rem;line-height:1.65}.base-camp-copy>p:first-child{margin-bottom:20px}
  .base-camp-highlights{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1.25rem}
  .base-camp-highlights article,.base-camp-schedule-grid article{min-width:0;text-align:center}
  .base-camp-highlights article{display:grid;grid-template-rows:3rem 5rem auto;align-content:start}
  .base-camp-highlights :global(svg),.base-camp-schedule-grid :global(svg){margin-bottom:.7rem;color:#94cdec}.base-camp-highlights :global(svg),.base-camp-schedule-grid :global(svg){margin-inline:auto}
  .base-camp-highlights h3,.base-camp-schedule-grid h3{margin:0 0 .55rem;color:#e4dda2;font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:calc(clamp(1.55rem,2.3vw,2.15rem) + var(--font-display-size-adjust));font-weight:600;line-height:1.03}
  .base-camp-highlights article p,.base-camp-schedule-grid article p{text-align:left}
  .base-camp-scheduling{padding-top:1.5rem;border-top:1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / .35)}
  .base-camp-subheading{color:#e4dda2;font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:calc(clamp(1.7rem,2.7vw,2.4rem) + var(--font-display-size-adjust))!important;font-weight:600;line-height:1.05}
  .base-camp-schedule-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1.5rem;margin-top:1.25rem}
  .base-camp :global(.button){margin-top:2rem;border-color:white;background:white;color:var(--color-forest-dark)}
  .reason-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;max-width:var(--width-wide);margin-inline:auto}
  .reason{padding:0;border:0;border-top:1px solid rgb(23 59 42 / .45);border-radius:0;background:transparent;box-shadow:none}
  .reason:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid rgb(23 59 42 / .45)}
